CONTEXT: When 300 models deliberate in clusters of 10, minority positions from small clusters get drowned by majority clusters during aggregation. The fleet converged on: logarithmic + inverse-frequency weighting to amplify rare positions.

YOUR COMPONENT: Write a Node.js module (city-minority-amplifier.js) that:
1. Takes an array of cluster outputs (each with convergedClaims, contestedPoints, minorityPositions)
2. Applies logarithmic weighting: positions held by fewer clusters get amplified (inverse-frequency)
3. Tracks which positions survived deliberation (BEDROCK/HELD) vs which were BROKEN across clusters
4. Ensures positions that appear in only 1-2 clusters but hit BEDROCK are NOT dropped — they carry forward with amplified weight
5. Returns: { amplifiedPositions, droppedPositions, diversityScore, minorityReport }
6. Exports: amplifyMinorities(clusterOutputs, carryOverThreshold=0.1), computeDiversityScore(positions), generateMinorityReport(clusterOutputs)

